		},
		{
			"type": "text",
			"version": 146,
			"x": 44.62084064981029,
			"y": 2388.4170804833752,
			"width": 584.380126953125,
			"height": 135,
			"strokeColor": "#8b949e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"text": "📝 Summary: What makes this work\n\n1. Trie = pre-built structure of all valid function names (guarantees validity)\n2. Masking = blocks invalid tokens by setting logits to -inf (ensures compliance)\n3. Model = chooses the best valid option based on the prompt (provides intelligence)\n4. Terminal detection = stops generation when a complete name is formed (avoids over-generation)\n5. Fallback = handles edge cases gracefully (ensures robustness)\n\n🟢 Result: 100% valid function names, every time!",
			"fontSize": 12,
			"fontFamily": 1,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"id": "summary",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"elementType": "text",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "📝 Summary: What makes this work\n\n1. Trie = pre-built structure of all valid function names (guarantees validity)\n2. Masking = blocks invalid tokens by setting logits to -inf (ensures compliance)\n3. Model = chooses the best valid option based on the prompt (provides intelligence)\n4. Terminal detection = stops generation when a complete name is formed (avoids over-generation)\n5. Fallback = handles edge cases gracefully (ensures robustness)\n\n🟢 Result: 100% valid function names, every time!",
